spans.s:
. २४.
the wherefrom and why of the ceremony is questioned for answer; ceremony for dis- liked पितृस् will be enjoyed by the राक्षसस् and दानवस्; tends to the growth of Soma who is the cause of the world growth; three पिण्डस् according to name and gotra; पितृस् give all including knowledge; at the तीर्थस् and rivers; बृहस्पति on श्राद्ध; once there was a thick haze of darkness in all worlds when ब्रह्मा engaged himself in yoga and created the worlds, सन्तानक and the first gods वैराजास्; the form- less groups of Gods attained absolution through yoga which is the strength of the पितृस्; and through this yoga Soma increases in power; hence feed thousands learned in the Vedic lore; feeding of a स्नातक equals that of many; atheists and the unrighteous should not be fed;
2: Ib.

; M. २०. 6; २१. ३३.
to be performed with faith using silver or silver-coated vessels and the Purodha to be given स्वधा; health and wealth are the fruits; superior to deva worship; even gods propitiate the पितृस् as also sages and other semi-divine beings; for योगैश्वर्य or मोक्ष- dharma;
3: Ib. III. १०. १००; M. १५. ३१.
details of the vedi and offerings during स्राद्धस्; पितृस् eat in the guise of वायु; offerings in Agni when it burns, otherwise it will lead to the blinding of eyes;
4: Ib. III. ११. 6, ४९, १००.
the ruling of बृहस्पति that first offerings are to be made to पिण्ड and then feeding Brahmans; by offering once the पितृस् become pleased;
5: Ib. III. १२. २६; १३. 1; M. १०. ३४.
the eclipse day good for; a list of articles to be used or discarded; women in their period unfit for [page३-477+ ४५] श्राद्ध; त्रिशङ्कु country, that of कारस्कर, कलिङ्ग and that of North of Sindhu unfit for श्राद्ध; naked persons must not be seen in a श्राद्ध; those who have no आश्रमस् are not fit for श्राद्ध; unfit to be seen then are dogs, fowls, hemophrodites, etc.; importance of शौचम् in a श्राद्ध;
6: Ib. III. १

.
हविस् of sesamum, rice, fruits and roots, flesh of animals and birds like fish, deer, hare, parrots, hog, छागल, gavya, aura- bhra, खड्ग, etc.; three Brahmans to be fed representing the trinity; not to feed those addicted to liquor, cattle rear- ing, and are messengers of villages, merchants; also one who picks up quarrels with parents, whose wife is in periods, a thief, one insulting friends, mad, hemophrodite, culpable of child murder, defiler of preceptor's bed, physician, adulterer, seller of Vedic Niyamas, dogs and brahmicides not to be seen in a श्राद्ध; the sprinkling of seasamum is to ward off Asuras and रक्षसस् from taking part; the time is the fore- noon of शुक्लपक्ष and afternoon of कृष्णपक्ष;
११: Ib. III. १९. 2.
offering of पिण्डस्; thus said बृहस्पति to his son in the श्राद्ध कल्प;
१२: २०. १०;

. ५३.
ordained for पितृस्; places for oblations in the absence of fire; articles fit and unfit for;
